That's odd, because I've always found archeologists relatively easy to play, not
to mention fun.  They advance to expert with the most powerful base weapon type
in the game (pickaxe) _as well as_ arguably the best artifact weapon type in the
game (saber), they can fight with two weapons, they're good with spells, they
get reasonable HP/power per level increases and they can make considerable
quantities of money in the early game both by burgling magic memory vaults and
selling identified gems.

The only real 'tricks' I can think of would be trading up the useless clothes
you start off with as early as possible, and dumping the bullwhip in favour of
the pickaxe as a primary weapon for the first part of the game.  I generally
make obtaining Grayswandir a priority (sacfesting as a lawful, otherwise I just
hold off against introducing new artifacts into the game until I get a wish),
and then pair it with a common or garden silver saber.

